// A value passed to a contract PARAMETER that it does not implement. This passed `kama check` clean and
// was refused by clang, naming `_Fx__Plain__as_Hashable` — a symbol the author never wrote, in generated
// code they never saw. The headline shape of the analysis gap, one position over from where it was
// already fixed.
//
// The cause was visible at the site: the argument hand-off skips the KIND rule when the parameter is a
// contract, and rightly — a contract admits every kind by design, which is what makes `hashVia(h: 22)`
// over a primitive a shipped feature (tests/intrinsic_widen.kama). But nothing was put in its place, so
// the one position that skipped the kind check checked nothing at all.
type value Plain { public int32 v = 0; public ctor make() { this.v = 0; } }

fn uint64 hashVia(Hashable h) { return h.hash(); }

fn int32 main()
{
    Plain p = Plain.make();
    return cast<int32>(hashVia(h: p));
}
